1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,700
We've been fighting every day, every night, because we currently have half a million lives in the balance.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:12,760
Half a million Haitians who have been calling these United States of ours home.

3
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:18,080
Some of them, two years, four years, many of us, 20 plus.

4
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:29,320
Coming tomorrow, if we do not get a redesignation, an extension of TPS for Haitians,

5
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:36,240
we are going to start one of the major family separations in modern history.

6
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:45,880
We are going to see over 100,000 U.S.-born children being ripped from their families.

7
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:58,800
We are going to witness those children when their parents are kidnapped, taken, and deported without any support.

8
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:07,520
What we are asking, and demanding, and urging, and praying for is to keep those families together.

9
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:19,890
What we are asking, and praying, and asking of those Haitian brothers and sisters who have become our neighbor.

10
00:01:19,890 --> 00:01:28,930
So as we continue to push, we have currently asking the President to please reconsider.

11
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:35,250
And we are urging him tomorrow to redesignate an extension of TPS for Haiti.

12
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:42,310
We have been called for such a time as this to protect those who have nowhere else to go.

13
00:01:42,610 --> 00:01:44,470
They cannot go back to Haiti.

14
00:01:45,050 --> 00:01:48,210
So it is our duty to fight for freedom.

15
00:01:48,550 --> 00:01:51,170
It is our duty to continue to push.

16
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:52,090
Thank you so much.

17
00:01:52,090 --> 00:01:52,570
Thank you.

